maya: FYI I hit a weird combo with the JS SDK -> edge runtimes (Bun/Deno). On a 401 retry the Authorization header disappears on the second fetch.

sam: Ugh. Minimal repro?

maya: Yep. Using import_map in Deno to point at our ESM build, but Bun sometimes resolves the CJS shim through conditional exports. Flow: initial fetch -> 401 -> refresh token -> mutate opts.headers and fetch again. Server sees no Authorization on the retry.

maya: Snippet:```js
async function retryFetch(url, opts){
  const r = await fetch(url, opts);
  if(r.status === 401){
    const token = await refreshToken();
    opts.headers = { ...opts.headers, Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }
    return fetch(url, opts) // second call loses header in Bun/Deno
  }
  return r;
}
```

li: Sounds like a classic Headers/Request consumption issue. Many runtimes treat existing Headers/Request as single-use. Workaround: clone headers before changing them. Eg:```js
const h = new Headers(opts.headers || {});
h.set('Authorization', `Bearer ${token}`);
return fetch(url, { ...opts, headers: h });
```

tasha: Also our Bun shim did `globalThis.fetch = (p,o) => nativeFetch(new Request(p,o))` which can drain streams/headers. Safer to call `nativeFetch(p, { ...o, headers: new Headers(o?.headers) })` instead.

sam: Good catches. Could be conditional-exports resolution differences causing different retry helpers to run in edge vs node builds. We should add a tiny cloneHeaders util exported from ESM so both paths share it.

maya: I implemented cloneHeaders(headers: HeadersInit) -> Headers and wired all retry paths to use it. Local tests fixed the repro for Bun and Deno.

infra-bot: Created RED-DEVEX-472: "preserve headers on retry across edge runtimes" and opened PR https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/pull/842 (adds cloneHeaders util, updates Bun shim, adds deno/bun integration test).

sam: Add an integration test that runs the repro under Bun and Deno (optional CI matrix) and a short changelog note under "compatibility fixes". Also ensure the util accepts Headers | Record<string,string> for TS callers.

maya: Will add tests and changelog. Thanks for the quick feedback.

li: Thanks for the detailed repro, saved a lot of time. :+1:
